      "narrative": "Maricopa County\u2019s residential market is flat to slightly down on prices, with Redfin reporting a median sale price of $484,000, down 0.81% year over year over the three months ending May 2026.[2] Inventory has come off recent highs but remains relatively elevated, with a county-level estimate of 4.19 months of supply and a median days on market of 42, indicating a more balanced environment than the aggressive seller\u2019s market of 2021-2022.[9] Homes are still selling, with 6,129 sales in May 2026, up from 5,554 a year earlier, and a 97.9% sale-to-list ratio, suggesting buyers have more negotiating room but competitively priced listings still attract solid demand.[2] Local dynamics continue to be shaped by strong population and job growth in Greater Phoenix, with county planning documents highlighting rapid growth, limited vacant residential land, and a persistent affordability gap as structural drivers of ongoing housing demand and development pressure.[4]",
