      "narrative": "Pima County\u2019s residential market is currently tilted toward sellers, with demand outpacing available listings and contract activity running well above last year.[2][1] Median sale prices in the broader Tucson area are roughly flat to slightly up year over year, with citywide prices near $320,000 for the three months ending May 2026, down about 1.6% from a year earlier, while some submarkets show modest price gains.[6][7] Inventory remains relatively tight, with one recent update reporting 4,248 active listings in Pima County, down more than 7% from a year earlier and new listings 15% below year-ago levels, leading to more competition among buyers even as many sellers are still making price reductions.[2][1] Locally, growth in the Sonoran Corridor and large new projects such as the ~2,000-home Camino Verano master plan south of Tucson International Airport are notable drivers, reflecting expanding employment and construction activity in that corridor.[6]",
